.SS "void csmp::IsoparametricLinearPyramid::dNr (double r, double s, double t, std::vector< double > & dNr) const\fR [virtual]\fP"
This method and the complementary method \fBdNs()\fP compute the shape function derivates with respect to the local coordinate axis 'r', and 's'\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The method takes the local coordinates of the point at which the shape function derivatives shall be evaluated as third argument\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIDNR\fP is the return value, i\&.e\&. a vector with the local-coordinate system interpolation function derivates in the local r coordinate direction\&.
.RE
.PP
The shape function derivatives are returned into the second method argument which is a floating point vector of the size n=nodes per element\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
see inlined source code in the header file\&.
